"""The game's sound effects, generated by ElevenLabs (Sound Effects v2), one or two takes each.

    python3 tools/sfx.py <downloads> assets/sounds        (needs ffmpeg)

The owner asked for every sound effect to be made again with ElevenLabs, cheaply (2026-11-13): one take where one
does, two where a sound is heard often enough that the same one twice would show (shots, blows, steps). Every
generation is on the ElevenLabs flow FLOW; TAKES keeps which generation each file is, so building again is a
download from that flow and never another charge. `<downloads>` holds the takes as `<file>.mp3`, as downloaded.

Each is made one channel, set to one loudness (the level the game's gains were tuned to with the old recordings),
its silent tail cut (but not a loop's: it has to meet its own start), and written as Ogg Vorbis, with
`manifest.json` ({ name: [file, ...] }) and `CREDITS.md`. Replaces what tools/sounds.py wrote there.
"""

